{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact TG-1 head c5bbd37f5b37f354e122a4d76c2bc5b7f6fcbce8, tree 3cd4aca4, on builder/native-scope-split-tg1-20261110, all 16 artifacts, for request 6a3a7fcc under promise af287821 and review request c8702131. The Native `scope` project is split into two ordered projects, `scope` and `scope-stories`. Every Native case still runs exactly once, and no runtime setting changes.\n\nWhat I checked in the source:\n\n- The split. `scope` drops its extra include list and keeps the package's own `test/**/*.test.ts`. `scope-stories` extends the same `packages/scope/vitest.worker.config.ts` and the same root. It adds the four story globs (lanes, CLI, Page and MCP) and excludes `test/**/*.test.ts`. The inherited config still excludes the denial file, the Lending file and `scopeScaleFiles`, so the lanes partition owner stays in `scope-scale` alone. Both projects take the shared `scopeProvide`, and the recorders still run only under `PAGE_RECORD=1` or `DEMO_RECORD=1`.\n- Unchanged settings. `isolate: false`, `maxWorkers: 2` and `testTimeout: 30_000` come from the inherited config, and the head does not change it. No pool option, heap flag or deadline changes. The group orders run from 1 to 5, and `testOptions` checks the five Native names in order.\n- The selectors. The two recorders in `recorder-output.ts`, the J3 runner and its config, `actor-cards.ts` and the two README examples now name `scope-stories`, as ruling a0997fbc allows. `test-summary.mjs` names the five Native projects once. `test-phases.test.mjs` now checks the include and exclude of `scope-stories`, and that `scope` has no include of its own. The remaining `--project scope` commands in `docs/contribute.md`, `docs/testing.md` and the CLI defect test select Scope package files, or are the comment and the Lending example that the note names.\n- The docs. `docs/testing-reference.md` describes the five Native groups, their workers and their order, and moves each story command to `scope-stories`.\n\nEvidence and digests:\n\n- Scope. Main 73e30699 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 16 paths that its 16 artifacts cover. The commit-message check passes: 8 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean, and `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. From gate head c95bc118 to the head, only the note and the four manifests change.\n- The manifests. The final gate manifest hashes to 6cdf7e49…1e70, and the static manifest hashes to 7f3caf26…0f30, as the request and booking c6b03c4a state. The three unit files match their recorded SHA-256 values, sizes and mode 0400, and `SHA256SUMS` verifies. The private manifest hashes to ec77ecc9…, as recorded.\n- The gate. The manifest names head c95bc118 and tree 92cdd6ef, which is c95bc118's tree. `gate.exit` and `driver.exit` read \"exit 0\". The test log reports 380 Plain files with 4,509 tests passed and one skipped, and 290 Native files passed and one skipped, with 1,134 tests passed and two skipped. It has no SIGBUS, fatal JavaScript error, heap exhaustion or unexpected Worker exit.\n- The counts. Main ran 284 owners and 1,127 cases in `scope`. With F, the head runs 190 owners and 796 cases in `scope` and 95 owners and 332 cases in `scope-stories`. Lending, denial and scale keep 1, 1 and 4 owners. The Native total stays 291 owners and 1,136 cases, so no owner moved twice or vanished.\n- The browser. GitHub reports Page run 42944496863 and Card run 42944500401 as attempt 1, successful, at c95bc118.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The split separates two kinds of owners that shared one runtime pool: the package's functional tests and the stories that load the whole Worker. It does so in the one file that defines projects, without touching a test or a runtime option. The ordered groups keep each runtime's life to its own project.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The change touches test projects, test scripts and documents. No product source, credential, route or setting changes.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Two notes:\n\n- One passing gate shows that the split works. It does not show that a runtime now stays under the 12-minute life the request names. The largest workerd sample, PID 60052 at 2,374,752 KiB, exceeds the 2,352,208 KiB of the PID that aborted at 43e9b328, and the note marks every lifetime as unknown. A gate that records each workerd PID's start and end would show the margin.\n- The CLI defect test's comment and the Lending example still give the old command, as the note says. A later head can correct them with the next change to those files.\n\nThis approval authorizes no deployment. G has the next local validation slot, and the planner decides the landing order.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bb08cc353c6171f029c620ea678224629d6487dd","binding":"assigned","head":"c5bbd37f5b37f354e122a4d76c2bc5b7f6fcbce8","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e3739180f91721f40bb0ea7ed75ebca7e0249e83\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:af287821038111e452959ff3e62c5dd612cc7dae\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:58486e75528cc6acf6f5731f230756fee1ea7b3b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}